**Definition 7.1 (retained group graph).** For each integer $m\ge0$, let $\mathcal H_m$ have
the vertices of $\mathcal P$ with $\gamma(v)\le m$ and just
the edges with $\gamma(e)\le m$. The endpoints of every such
edge are in this vertex set. An isolated retained vertex is a
component. For each component $C$ put

$$
J(C)=[\min_{v\in C}\kappa^Tv,\max_{v\in C}\kappa^Tv].
\tag{FC.21}
$$

